DEFINITIONS

  "Licensor"  Saba Sabashvili.
  "Software"  The contents of this repository, in source or compiled form,
              including its documentation.
  "You"       The individual or legal entity exercising the permissions below.
  "Production Use"  Any use that is not Evaluation Use, including use in the
              operation of a business or in the handling of real credentials.
  "Evaluation Use"  Running the Software in order to assess it, using data that
              is not real.
  "Licensed Capabilities"  The following six capabilities, and only these:
              (i)   single sign-on via OIDC;
              (ii)  sealing the master key with an external KMS;
              (iii) Redis-backed high availability across replicas;
              (iv)  dynamic secrets (credentials minted per lease);
              (v)   managed rotation of secrets held in external systems;
              (vi)  signed audit attestation.
  "Community Use"  Production Use of the Software that does not use any
              Licensed Capability.

GRANT

  1. Community. You may download, read, compile, run, and put the Software to
     Community Use, free of charge, for an unlimited period, on any number of
     deployments, for any number of users, including in the operation of a
     business and to hold real credentials. No payment, registration, or
     licence key is required, and the Software transmits nothing to the
     Licensor.

  2. Evaluation of Licensed Capabilities. You may use the Licensed Capabilities
     for Evaluation Use, and for up to 30 consecutive days of Production Use, in
     order to assess them.

  3. Production use of Licensed Capabilities. Beyond the period in section 2,
     You may not use a Licensed Capability in Production Use except under a
     commercial licence obtained from the Licensor. The commercial terms
     accompanying that licence define its term, scope, support, and warranties.

  4. Modification. You may modify the Software for Your own Community Use or
     Evaluation Use, and under a commercial licence to the extent that licence
     permits. Modifying it does not grant You any right to distribute it.

  5. No technical enforcement. The Software does not disable, degrade, or block
     any capability when unlicensed, and never withholds access to Your own
     data. This is deliberate and permanent. It is not a waiver: a capability
     that continues to run is not thereby licensed, and section 3 governs.

